// trap: a move into the class of its own source, a loop the stored graph keeps as a loop.
// One ticket, two desks alike: Reassign moves the ticket to the other desk, and the state it
// reaches is the one it left with the desks swapped, so a run up to instance symmetry stores
// the move as a loop (an orbit self-edge). Close ends the ticket at the desk that holds it,
// but nothing makes it run: under WF_vars(Next) the ticket may be reassigned forever, so
// TicketCloses fails, by a lasso that reassigns the ticket there and back. A checker that
// read the loop as a stutter would find no cycle, let Close end every behavior, and answer
// ok. `.fair(Close)` is fair per (ticket, desk), since Close binds the desk it writes: each
// reassignment disables the instance of the desk the ticket left, so the same loop is fair
// and TicketClosesFair fails too. A checker that kept the instance's desk where it was
// around the loop would find it enabled throughout and never taken, and answer ok.
// flags: --instances Ticket=1
// expect TicketCloses: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample
// expect TicketClosesFair: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample
entity Desk "窓口" { id: Int @pk  open: Bool @default(true) }
entity Ticket "問合せ" { id: Int @pk  status: Enum(open, closed) @default(open) }
relate(Ticket, Desk, N:1)
usecase Staff "開設"
usecase Raise "受付"
usecase Reassign "担当替え"
usecase Close "完了"
creates(Staff, Desk)
creates(Raise, Ticket)
relinks(Reassign, Ticket, Desk)
transitions(Close, Ticket.status, open -> closed)
sets(Close, Desk.open == true)
condition HoldsTicket "未完了の問合せを持つ窓口"
holds(HoldsTicket, Desk.open == true).has(Ticket.status == open)
applies_to(HoldsTicket, Close)
property TicketCloses leads_to(Ticket.status == open, Ticket.status == closed)
property TicketClosesFair leads_to(Ticket.status == open, Ticket.status == closed).fair(Close)
